From 1a2f871eb0256533e410a9e23521712ef75b3981 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Adam Benhassen <adambenhassen@hotmail.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 01:05:06 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] feat(qwen3.5): runtime rank-1 refusal projection with
 per-request lambda

Project each residual writer's output (linear_attn.out_proj, self_attn.o_proj,
mlp.down_proj) with y - lambda * coef * r (r . y), loaded from
VLLM_REFUSAL_DIRS. Port of pocharlies-org/qwen38-27b-rank1-refusal-projection
(Apache-2.0) to this fork's V2 model runner.

- Per request via cache_salt "refusal:<x>"; global via
  POST /admin/refusal_lambda, which resets the prefix cache and returns 409
  while requests hold KV.
- lambda and the per-token buffer are module buffers mutated in place, so
  CUDA graphs and AOT-loaded artifacts read live values.
- VLLM_REFUSAL_DIRS joins the compile hash; fails closed on unclaimed or
  double-claimed directions. The MTP drafter is not projected.
